{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.67b95f5815","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_compare","group":"syn-c-323","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Valewood National Park is in southern Brazil. It was established in 1894.</li><li>Its area is 6,025 square kilometers.</li><li>Fenwick National Park is in eastern Poland. It was established in 1998.</li><li>Its area is 5,087 square kilometers.</li><li>Both are parks that protect coastal wetlands.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast when the two parks were established.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Both Valewood National Park and Fenwick National Park are parks that protect coastal wetlands.","The area of Valewood National Park (6,025 square kilometers) is greater than that of Fenwick National Park (5,087 square kilometers).","Valewood National Park was established in 1894, while Fenwick National Park was established in 1998.","Valewood National Park is in southern Brazil, and Fenwick National Park is in eastern Poland."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It gives both dates and contrasts them. The other choices compare size or location, or describe a similarity."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.bfa1bafee4","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_compare","group":"syn-c-336","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Mount Juniper is in western Kenya. It was first climbed in 1892.</li><li>Its height is 6,115 meters.</li><li>Mount Cresthill is in eastern Australia. It was first climbed in 1964.</li><li>Its height is 5,586 meters.</li><li>Both are peaks in the same mountain range.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast when the two mountains were first climbed.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The height of Mount Juniper (6,115 meters) is greater than that of Mount Cresthill (5,586 meters).","Mount Juniper was first climbed in 1892, while Mount Cresthill was first climbed in 1964.","Mount Juniper is in western Kenya, and Mount Cresthill is in eastern Australia.","Both Mount Juniper and Mount Cresthill are peaks in the same mountain range."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It gives both dates and contrasts them. The other choices compare size or location, or describe a similarity."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.754825a561","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_compare","group":"syn-c-345","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Fenwick Observatory is in western Kenya. It began operating in 1925.</li><li>Its main telescope's mirror diameter is 10 meters.</li><li>The Cresthill Observatory is in southern New Zealand. It began operating in 1912.</li><li>Its main telescope's mirror diameter is 6 meters.</li><li>Both are observatories located on remote mountaintops.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast when the two observatorys began operating.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Fenwick Observatory began operating in 1925, while the Cresthill Observatory began operating in 1912.","Both the Fenwick Observatory and the Cresthill Observatory are observatories located on remote mountaintops.","The Fenwick Observatory is in western Kenya, and the Cresthill Observatory is in southern New Zealand.","The main telescope's mirror diameter of the Fenwick Observatory (10 meters) is greater than that of the Cresthill Observatory (6 meters)."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It gives both dates and contrasts them. The other choices compare size or location, or describe a similarity."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.2839322849","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_compare","group":"syn-c-351","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Eastwick National Park is in central Canada. It was established in 1969.</li><li>Its area is 6,719 square kilometers.</li><li>Wexford National Park is in eastern Australia. It was established in 1962.</li><li>Its area is 6,346 square kilometers.</li><li>Both are parks known for their old-growth forests.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize a similarity between Eastwick National Park and Wexford National Park.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Both Eastwick National Park and Wexford National Park are parks known for their old-growth forests.","Eastwick National Park is in central Canada, and Wexford National Park is in eastern Australia.","The area of Eastwick National Park (6,719 square kilometers) is greater than that of Wexford National Park (6,346 square kilometers).","Eastwick National Park was established in 1969, while Wexford National Park was established in 1962."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. Only this choice describes something the two share. The others present differences (in size, date, or location)."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.2627414949","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_compare","group":"syn-c-364","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Mount Pembrook is in eastern Australia. It was first climbed in 1896.</li><li>Its height is 4,855 meters.</li><li>Mount Glenrock is in eastern Poland. It was first climbed in 2017.</li><li>Its height is 2,124 meters.</li><li>Both are dormant volcanoes.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize how the height of the two mountains differs.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Mount Pembrook, which is in eastern Australia, is one of several dormant volcanoes.","Both Mount Pembrook and Mount Glenrock are dormant volcanoes.","Mount Pembrook was first climbed in 1896, while Mount Glenrock was first climbed in 2017.","The height of Mount Pembrook (4,855 meters) is greater than that of Mount Glenrock (2,124 meters)."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It compares the height of both mountains. The other choices describe a similarity, a difference in date, or only one mountain."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.648083b729","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_compare","group":"syn-c-370","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Mount Fenwick is in western Scotland. It was first climbed in 2011.</li><li>Its height is 3,274 meters.</li><li>Mount Sable is in southern Brazil. It was first climbed in 1999.</li><li>Its height is 2,694 meters.</li><li>Both are dormant volcanoes.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two mountains.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Mount Fenwick, which is in western Scotland, is one of several dormant volcanoes.","The height of Mount Fenwick (3,274 meters) is greater than that of Mount Sable (2,694 meters).","Mount Fenwick is in western Scotland, and Mount Sable is in southern Brazil.","Mount Fenwick was first climbed in 2011, while Mount Sable was first climbed in 1999."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.20942c075a","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_compare","group":"syn-c-377","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Glenrock Observatory is in northern Chile. It began operating in 1909.</li><li>Its main telescope's mirror diameter is 11 meters.</li><li>The Eastwick Observatory is in southern New Zealand. It began operating in 1963.</li><li>Its main telescope's mirror diameter is 2 meters.</li><li>Both are observatories located on remote mountaintops.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two observatorys.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Glenrock Observatory, which is in northern Chile, is one of several observatories located on remote mountaintops.","The Glenrock Observatory began operating in 1909, while the Eastwick Observatory began operating in 1963.","The main telescope's mirror diameter of the Glenrock Observatory (11 meters) is greater than that of the Eastwick Observatory (2 meters).","The Glenrock Observatory is in northern Chile, and the Eastwick Observatory is in southern New Zealand."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.22175118c9","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_compare","group":"syn-c-384","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Lake Larkspur is in western Scotland. It was first surveyed in 1899.</li><li>Its surface area is 523 square kilometers.</li><li>Lake Brookhaven is in southern Norway. It was first surveyed in 1912.</li><li>Its surface area is 394 square kilometers.</li><li>Both are reservoirs created by dams.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two lakes.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The surface area of Lake Larkspur (523 square kilometers) is greater than that of Lake Brookhaven (394 square kilometers).","Lake Larkspur is in western Scotland, and Lake Brookhaven is in southern Norway.","Lake Larkspur, which is in western Scotland, is one of several reservoirs created by dams.","Lake Larkspur was first surveyed in 1899, while Lake Brookhaven was first surveyed in 1912."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.6e5c575d55","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-8","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Lucía Sato is an ecologist.</li><li>Sato wanted to find out whether city lights change when songbirds begin singing in the morning.</li><li>Sato compared the first songs of robins in brightly lit city parks with those in dark rural woodlands.</li><li>Sato found that robins in lit parks began singing nearly an hour earlier.</li><li>Sato concluded that artificial light may shift birds' daily rhythms.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Sato found that robins in lit parks began singing nearly an hour earlier.","Ecologist Lucía Sato set out to learn whether city lights change when songbirds begin singing in the morning.","Sato concluded that artificial light may shift birds' daily rhythms.","To investigate the question, Sato compared the first songs of robins in brightly lit city parks with those in dark rural woodlands."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.fa684f463e","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-18","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Diego Haddad is an agricultural scientist.</li><li>Haddad wanted to find out whether planting clover between rows of corn reduces the need for fertilizer.</li><li>Haddad grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons.</li><li>Haddad found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer.</li><li>Haddad concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Haddad grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons.","Haddad found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer.","Haddad concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.","Agricultural scientist Diego Haddad set out to learn whether planting clover between rows of corn reduces the need for fertilizer."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.d09004f165","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-19","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Zara Halvorsen is an agricultural scientist.</li><li>Halvorsen wanted to find out whether planting clover between rows of corn reduces the need for fertilizer.</li><li>Halvorsen grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons.</li><li>Halvorsen found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer.</li><li>Halvorsen concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Agricultural scientist Zara Halvorsen set out to learn whether planting clover between rows of corn reduces the need for fertilizer.","Halvorsen concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.","To investigate the question, Halvorsen grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons.","Halvorsen found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.64251b1ab5","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-19","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Zara Halvorsen is an agricultural scientist.</li><li>Halvorsen wanted to find out whether planting clover between rows of corn reduces the need for fertilizer.</li><li>Halvorsen grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons.</li><li>Halvorsen found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer.</li><li>Halvorsen concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer, Halvorsen concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.","Halvorsen found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer.","Halvorsen concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.","To investigate the question, Halvorsen grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.b4adf03394","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-30","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Yara Nakamura is an entomologist.</li><li>Nakamura wanted to find out whether bees prefer flowers of a particular color.</li><li>Nakamura set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow.</li><li>Nakamura found that bees visited the blue feeders most often.</li><li>Nakamura concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Entomologist Yara Nakamura set out to learn whether bees prefer flowers of a particular color.","Nakamura concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.","Nakamura found that bees visited the blue feeders most often.","To investigate the question, Nakamura set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.2a92d96ee1","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-33","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Idris Solberg is an entomologist.</li><li>Solberg wanted to find out whether bees prefer flowers of a particular color.</li><li>Solberg set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow.</li><li>Solberg found that bees visited the blue feeders most often.</li><li>Solberg concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Solberg concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.","Because bees visited the blue feeders most often, Solberg concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.","Solberg found that bees visited the blue feeders most often.","To investigate the question, Solberg set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.cb222dd02b","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-35","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Dmitri Solberg is an entomologist.</li><li>Solberg wanted to find out whether bees prefer flowers of a particular color.</li><li>Solberg set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow.</li><li>Solberg found that bees visited the blue feeders most often.</li><li>Solberg concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Solberg found that bees visited the blue feeders most often.","To investigate the question, Solberg set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow.","Entomologist Dmitri Solberg set out to learn whether bees prefer flowers of a particular color.","Solberg concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.8d6269722b","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-35","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Dmitri Solberg is an entomologist.</li><li>Solberg wanted to find out whether bees prefer flowers of a particular color.</li><li>Solberg set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow.</li><li>Solberg found that bees visited the blue feeders most often.</li><li>Solberg concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Solberg set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow.","Solberg concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.","Solberg found that bees visited the blue feeders most often.","Because bees visited the blue feeders most often, Solberg concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.b332559ba6","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-39","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kofi Kowalski is a sociologist.</li><li>Kowalski wanted to find out whether community gardens increase how often neighbors talk to one another.</li><li>Kowalski surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods.</li><li>Kowalski found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened.</li><li>Kowalski concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Kowalski concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.","Kowalski found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened.","To investigate the question, Kowalski surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods.","Sociologist Kofi Kowalski set out to learn whether community gardens increase how often neighbors talk to one another."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.8eff3ea0fb","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-47","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Dmitri Mensah is a geologist.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether a hillside's plant cover affects how much soil washes away in heavy rain.</li><li>Mensah measured soil runoff on bare slopes and on slopes covered with native grasses.</li><li>Mensah found that bare slopes lost several times more soil.</li><li>Mensah concluded that plant cover may protect hillsides from erosion.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Geologist Dmitri Mensah set out to learn whether a hillside's plant cover affects how much soil washes away in heavy rain.","To investigate the question, Mensah measured soil runoff on bare slopes and on slopes covered with native grasses.","Mensah concluded that plant cover may protect hillsides from erosion.","Mensah found that bare slopes lost several times more soil."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.0617657af5","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-58","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Diego Iyer is a zoologist.</li><li>Iyer wanted to find out whether zoo elephants that are given puzzle feeders are more active.</li><li>Iyer gave puzzle feeders to some elephants and standard food trays to others, then tracked their movement.</li><li>Iyer found that elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day.</li><li>Iyer concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Zoologist Diego Iyer set out to learn whether zoo elephants that are given puzzle feeders are more active.","Iyer concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity.","Iyer found that elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day.","To investigate the question, Iyer gave puzzle feeders to some elephants and standard food trays to others, then tracked their movement."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.b33459ab51","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-77","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Nadia Duarte is an economist.</li><li>Duarte wanted to find out whether a four-day workweek changes employee productivity.</li><li>Duarte tracked output at companies before and after they adopted a four-day week.</li><li>Duarte found that output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly.</li><li>Duarte concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly, Duarte concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.","Duarte concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.","To investigate the question, Duarte tracked output at companies before and after they adopted a four-day week.","Duarte found that output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.1adead8001","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-100","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Lucía Sato is an education researcher.</li><li>Sato wanted to find out whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary.</li><li>Sato had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.</li><li>Sato found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.</li><li>Sato concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Sato concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.","Sato found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.","To investigate the question, Sato had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.","Education researcher Lucía Sato set out to learn whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.1dfd77fc8d","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-101","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Jonas Oyelaran is an education researcher.</li><li>Oyelaran wanted to find out whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary.</li><li>Oyelaran had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.</li><li>Oyelaran found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.</li><li>Oyelaran concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Oyelaran concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.","Oyelaran found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.","Education researcher Jonas Oyelaran set out to learn whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary.","To investigate the question, Oyelaran had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.d2cc3226bb","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-109","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Lucía Petrov is a primatologist.</li><li>Petrov wanted to find out whether young chimpanzees learn to use tools by watching adults.</li><li>Petrov observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.</li><li>Petrov found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.</li><li>Petrov concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Primatologist Lucía Petrov set out to learn whether young chimpanzees learn to use tools by watching adults.","Petrov found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.","To investigate the question, Petrov observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.","Petrov concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.f29bfe82cc","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-118","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Hana Ferreira is a sleep researcher.</li><li>Ferreira wanted to find out whether using screens before bed affects how quickly people fall asleep.</li><li>Ferreira asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed.</li><li>Ferreira found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep.</li><li>Ferreira concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Ferreira concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.","Ferreira found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep.","To investigate the question, Ferreira asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed.","Sleep researcher Hana Ferreira set out to learn whether using screens before bed affects how quickly people fall asleep."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.dfe559db7b","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-121","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Tomás Ferreira is an ornithologist.</li><li>Ferreira wanted to find out whether birds that migrate farther have longer wings.</li><li>Ferreira measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.</li><li>Ferreira found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.</li><li>Ferreira concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Ferreira concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.","To investigate the question, Ferreira measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.","Ornithologist Tomás Ferreira set out to learn whether birds that migrate farther have longer wings.","Ferreira found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.a90715def2","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-122","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ingrid Lindqvist is an ornithologist.</li><li>Lindqvist wanted to find out whether birds that migrate farther have longer wings.</li><li>Lindqvist measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.</li><li>Lindqvist found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.</li><li>Lindqvist concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings, Lindqvist concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.","Lindqvist concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.","To investigate the question, Lindqvist measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.","Lindqvist found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.a4b601b024","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-128","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Zara Moreau is a public health researcher.</li><li>Moreau wanted to find out whether adding bike lanes increases how often residents cycle.</li><li>Moreau counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added.</li><li>Moreau found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.</li><li>Moreau concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Moreau counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added.","Moreau concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.","Because cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year, Moreau concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.","Moreau found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.9dd64bc80b","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-131","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Samuel Novak is a public health researcher.</li><li>Novak wanted to find out whether adding bike lanes increases how often residents cycle.</li><li>Novak counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added.</li><li>Novak found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.</li><li>Novak concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year, Novak concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.","Novak concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.","Novak found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.","To investigate the question, Novak counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.eaab068d00","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-153","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Idris Nakamura is a climate scientist.</li><li>Nakamura wanted to find out whether light-colored roofs reduce indoor temperatures.</li><li>Nakamura compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs.</li><li>Nakamura found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.</li><li>Nakamura concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Nakamura found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.","Nakamura concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.","Climate scientist Idris Nakamura set out to learn whether light-colored roofs reduce indoor temperatures.","To investigate the question, Nakamura compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.62280280c8","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-165","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Lucía Ferreira is a veterinary scientist.</li><li>Ferreira wanted to find out whether dogs recognize their owners' voices.</li><li>Ferreira played recordings of owners' voices and strangers' voices to dogs.</li><li>Ferreira found that dogs turned toward their owners' voices far more often.</li><li>Ferreira concluded that dogs may be able to tell their owners' voices apart from others.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Ferreira concluded that dogs may be able to tell their owners' voices apart from others.","Ferreira found that dogs turned toward their owners' voices far more often.","Veterinary scientist Lucía Ferreira set out to learn whether dogs recognize their owners' voices.","To investigate the question, Ferreira played recordings of owners' voices and strangers' voices to dogs."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.cb5bff4d6f","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-170","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Adeyemi is a forest ecologist.</li><li>Adeyemi wanted to find out whether fungi help trees share nutrients.</li><li>Adeyemi added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.</li><li>Adeyemi found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.</li><li>Adeyemi concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Adeyemi added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.","Because the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks, Adeyemi concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.","Adeyemi found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.","Adeyemi concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.2ad2403e72","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-171","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Priya Varga is a forest ecologist.</li><li>Varga wanted to find out whether fungi help trees share nutrients.</li><li>Varga added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.</li><li>Varga found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.</li><li>Varga concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Varga added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.","Varga concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.","Forest ecologist Priya Varga set out to learn whether fungi help trees share nutrients.","Varga found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.4c4ef4163b","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-175","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Omar Nakamura is a music researcher.</li><li>Nakamura wanted to find out whether learning an instrument improves children's listening skills.</li><li>Nakamura tested children's ability to pick out sounds in noise before and after two years of music lessons.</li><li>Nakamura found that children who took lessons improved more than those who did not.</li><li>Nakamura concluded that music training may sharpen listening skills.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Music researcher Omar Nakamura set out to learn whether learning an instrument improves children's listening skills.","To investigate the question, Nakamura tested children's ability to pick out sounds in noise before and after two years of music lessons.","Nakamura found that children who took lessons improved more than those who did not.","Nakamura concluded that music training may sharpen listening skills."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."}
